content.text:
Fixed the single blocker from the review.

**What was wrong:** the FIG. 2 brief measured 2806 characters against a 2800 limit.

**What I did:** trimmed FIG-2.md by wording only, leaving every disclosed structure, relationship, numeral, and placement target intact:

- collapsed the repeated definite articles in the "shown schematically" sentence;
- shortened "the channel being divided" to "the channel divided";
- shortened "Part names here are semantic identifiers only" to "Part names are semantic identifiers only";
- removed the sentence pointing at FIG. 5, which was a cross-reference to a reader rather than geometry for the sheet. The corresponding cross-reference in the Brief Description of the Drawings is untouched.

The file is now 2781 characters as stored, comfortably under the limit under either the stored-file or body-only measure, so the trim will not sit on the threshold again.

I verified the rest stayed consistent rather than assuming it: FIG. 2 still lists 22, 24, 30, 36 and 66, each of those still has geometry in the brief and a placement target, each matches its single canonical part name in `draft/numerals.md`, and the two places in the specification that mention FIG. 2 (`draft/07-drawings.md:3` and `draft/08-detailed-description.md:21`) name only parts the sheet still carries. A sweep of `draft/` and `figures/` for unfinished markers and em dashes came back empty. No other figure brief is near the character limit. No text, claim, or numeral changed.
